because we call `app.Setup` now, and it creates a configz, we need to clean up this config for next test case, or just log the error and don't return directly

```
	if cz, err := configz.New("componentconfig"); err == nil {
		cz.Set(cc.ComponentConfig)
	} else {
		return nil, nil, fmt.Errorf("unable to register configz: %s", err)
	}
```

Actually, if we move this to `Run`, we still need to add `configz.Delete("componentconfig")` because `app.Run` is also called by `StartTestServer`.

We can find similar code in `cmd/kube-controller-manager/app/controllermanager.go` which also has a testserver used by `/pkg/integration/serving`

```
func Run(c *config.CompletedConfig, stopCh <-chan struct{}) error {
	// To help debugging, immediately log version
	klog.Infof("Version: %+v", version.Get())

	if cfgz, err := configz.New(ConfigzName); err == nil {
		cfgz.Set(c.ComponentConfig)
	} else {
		klog.Errorf("unable to register configz: %v", err)
	}
```

it logs an error and continue the execution, otherwise it will also need a `configz.Delete`
